# VGV workflow handoffs (Cursor)

This rule **does not replace** Wingspan skills. When `/brainstorm`, `/plan`,
`/build`, `/code-review`, or `/plan-technical-review` runs, **that skill's
SKILL.md is authoritative** for workflow steps and **AskQuestion options**
(Claude Code name: AskUserQuestion — always use **AskQuestion** in Cursor).

This rule only changes **how selections execute in Cursor** (same chat, no
`/clear`, no copy-paste slash lines).

## Cursor-native option lists

Always present options via the **AskQuestion** tool (clickable picker), never
as numbered chat text the user must type back. Upstream Claude lists a
"clear context" twin next to "start in place"; after the Cursor port those
are the same action, so present the **deduped** lists below.

**After brainstorm** (from brainstorm skill):

1. Plan now (Recommended)
2. Review and refine approach
3. Done for now

**After plan** (from plan skill — Wingspan ≥ v0.0.4):

1. Build now (Recommended)
2. Open the plan file in my code editor
3. Review and refine

**After plan-technical-review** — follow that skill's post-review options
(same dedupe: one Build now, not Start building).

**After build** — follow build skill post-ship options.

Never ask these as plain chat when AskQuestion is available. Never display a
"Clear context", "Start building", or "Continue with planning" action — those
are Claude twins of Plan now / Build now.

## AskQuestion availability

`AskQuestion` is host-injected. It is currently **unavailable on Grok 4.5**
(every mode). When the tool is missing from the session schema, fall back to a
short numbered chat list **silently** — no notice that the tool is absent, no
suggestion to switch models, no apology. See `vgv-ask-question.mdc` → *Degrade
silently*. The table below is agent routing guidance; do not recite it in chat.

## Parent model routing (preserve multi-model strength)

Use the **chat model picker** for the parent agent; subagent `model:` pins
are set by the link script from upstream Wingspan tiers:

| Phase / role | Recommended parent model | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Brainstorm / plan / refine (AskQuestion handoffs) | **Composer 2.5** | Clickable picker works; Cursor Models pool |
| Build / implementation | Composer 2.5 or Claude Sonnet 5 | Coding strength; user preference |
| Avoid for handoffs | **Grok 4.5** | No AskQuestion |

Subagent pins (do not override in the Task call unless the user asks):

| Upstream tier | Cursor `model:` | Agents |
| --- | --- | --- |
| haiku | `composer-2.5` | `pr-readiness-review-agent` |
| sonnet | `claude-sonnet-5` | codebase, simplicity, test-quality, plan-splitting, research agents |
| inherit | `inherit` | vgv-review, architecture, user-flow, flutter-reviewer |

That keeps mechanical checks cheap on Composer, deep reviews on Sonnet 5,
and orchestrator-aligned agents matching the parent.

## Cursor execution (when user picks an option)

Execute **immediately in this chat**. Do not output `/clear`, `/new-chat`,
suggest a context reset, or tell the user to copy-paste `/plan path` or
`/build path`.

| User selection | Cursor action |
| --- | --- |
| Plan now | Run **plan** skill on the brainstorm doc path |
| Build now | Run **build** skill on the plan file path |
| Open the plan file in my code editor | `open docs/plan/<filename>.md` |
| Review and refine / Review and refine approach | Run **refine-approach** on the artifact |
| Freeform: run plan-technical-review | Run **plan-technical-review** on the plan path |
| Review (after `/build`) | Run **code-review** on the changed scope |
| Done for now / Done | Summarize artifact path; stop |

## `/review` vs `/code-review` (Cursor)

| Command | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `/review` | Cursor built-in — Bugbot or Security only |
| `/code-review` | VGV Wingspan quality review (Claude `/review`) |

## Slash skills still available

Users can invoke `/plan`, `/build`, `/brainstorm`, `/code-review`, etc.
This rule does not remove slash commands — it fixes handoff **execution**
after phase completion.

## Skill locations

1. **Global (preferred):** `~/.cursor/skills/` — all Cursor projects
2. **Repo ports mirror:** `.cursor/skill-ports/` — regenerated by the
   link script (not scanned by Cursor; avoids duplicate slash skills)
3. **Repo fallback:** `.cursor/skills/` — created only if global is
   empty
4. **Custom skill sources:** `.cursor/skill-custom/` (Sea Trials only)

Re-run `./scripts/cursor-link-vgv-skills.sh` after `git pull`.

## Artifact YAML header

When writing new brainstorm or plan docs:

```yaml
vgv_next:
  skill: plan
  artifact: docs/brainstorm/YYYY-MM-DD-topic-brainstorm-doc.md
```

(or `skill: build` + plan path after planning)

User can `@`-attach the file and say: “Run the next skill from `vgv_next`.”

## Optional: thread too long

Only if the user **asks** for a fresh session: new chat (Cmd+L / Ctrl+L),
then `/` → skill → `@` artifact. Not the default handoff.

